title Widening the fence for one retry

model  "Model"
tool   "Shell tool"
person "Person"
fence  "Fence (workspace-write)"
cache  "~/.npm cache"

call1, call2 at model

# npm install runs fenced, and its write to ~/.npm is outside the allowed folders
pause "The fence allows writes only in the project and temp folders."

# The first try is refused by the fence
call1 -> tool
call1 -> fence : blocked "The kernel refuses the write to ~/.npm."
call1 -> model : failed "The result says access was denied and that one retry may ask."

# The model retries the same command with a wider mode and a reason
call2 -> tool : waiting "It names danger-full-access and gives one sentence for the person."

# The person reads the reason and allows it once
new ask at tool
ask -> person : waiting
ask : done "Only a clear yes widens anything."
ask -> tool
remove ask

# This one call skips the fence and the cache write succeeds
call2 -> cache : done "The wider mode is used for this call and stored nowhere."
call2 -> model "The next command is fenced again."
